===Verb===
{{en-verb|past2=learnt}}

# To [[acquire]], or attempt to acquire [[knowledge]] or an ability to do something.
#:''It's time Dad '''learn'''ed (how) to change the oil in the car''.
#:''In my latest job, I've '''learn'''t to keep my mouth shut more than in the last one''.
#:''Toddlers '''learn''' to walk at around one year old.''
#* {{RQ:Cowper Task
|passage=a school in which he '''learns''' sly circumvention}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=18-04-1987|journal=Gay Community News|page=7|author=Tom Grabosky|title=Gay Men's Voices Rise Up Singin'|text=I was very impressed with the obvious amount of work that went into the '''learning''' and synchronization of such a complex and harmonically and difficult score.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1988|author=Mark Andre Peter Loranc|title=A Study of the Ionospheric Signature of Ion Supply from the Ionosphere to the Magnetosphere|page=iv|text=I have '''learned''' far more from them about how to be a scientist than they realize. Above all else, they taught me the virtues of proper waterfowl alignment.|chapter=Acknowledgements|genre=PhD dissertation|location=University of Texas at Dallas}}
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20171014193917/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-6-where-is-the-gym/3225958.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: Every day I '''learn''' more about this great city.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 15, 2019|issue=10,188|page=5|author=Hugh Graham; Alice Hutton|title=Milk or tea first? Charles's butlers have the answer|work=The Sunday Times|passage=Other rules '''learnt''' by butlers include lighting candles 15 minutes before guests enter a room, and not saying "good morning" to guests until you are 5ft away.}}
# To [[attend]] a course or other [[educational]] activity.
#* {{RQ:Defoe Robinson Crusoe|passage=For, as he took delight to introduce me, I took delight to '''learn.'''}}
# To gain knowledge from a bad [[experience]] so as to [[improve]].
#: {{ux|en|'''learn''' from one's mistakes}}
# To [[study]].
#: {{ux|en|I '''learn''' medicine.}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''learn''' psychology.}}
# To come to [[know]]; to become [[inform]]ed of; to [[find out]].
#: {{ux|en|He just '''learned''' that he will be sacked.}}
# {{lb|en|now only in|_|non-standard speech|and|dialects}} To [[teach]].
#: {{ux|en|Give him a clip round the ear. That'll '''learn''' him!}}
#* {{RQ:Mlry MrtDrthr|10.9|2|VIII|ix|passage=And whan she had serched hym <br> she fond in the bottome of his wound that therin was poyson <br> And soo she heled hym{{...}}<br> and therfore Tramtrist cast grete loue to la beale Isoud <br> for she was at that tyme the fairest mayde and lady of the worlde <br> And there Tramtryst '''lerned''' her to harpe <br> and she beganne to haue grete fantasye vnto hym}}
<!--Prior quote:And there Tramtryste '''lerned''' hir to harpe, and she began to have a grete fantasy unto hym.-->
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Much Ado About Nothing Q|act=IV|scene=i|sig=F3|verso=1|page=49|passage=Sweete Prince, you '''learne''' me noble thankfulnes: {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Cymbeline|act=I|scene=v|page=373|column=1|passage=Haue I not bene <br> Thy Pupill long? Haſt thou not '''learn'd''' me how <br> To make Perfumes?}}
#* {{RQ:Bunyan Christian Behaviour|chapter=Touching Parents|page=56|passage={{...}} ''Take heed of filling their'' {{quote-gloss|''i.e.'', children's}} ''heads with VVhimzies, and unprofitable Notions''; for this vvill ſooner '''learn''' them to be malepert and proud, than ſober and humble.}}
